# 39. Performance

Let:

```text
Q = number of questions
C = average non-zero contributions per selected response
```

Scoring complexity is approximately:

```text
O(Q × C)
```

For an assessment-sized input, no evidence currently justifies:

- ETS caching;
- Redis;
- GenServers;
- distributed scoring;
- Rust/Rustler;
- parallel processing.

Correctness dominates micro-performance.

---

# 40. Future integration direction

If later adopted by NewYou:

```text
Phoenix/LiveView
→ authoritative Ash application action
→ Temperament Domain operation
→ pure scoring calculation
→ immutable durable result
```

The pure scorer remains calculation machinery.

It must not become a second owner of Temperament business truth.

---

# 41. Technical success criteria

The technical design is successful when one engine can prove:

```text
book-compatible scoring
weighted calculation
mixed response formats
randomised presentation invariance
exact ties
explainability
determinism
safe validation
```

without infrastructure dependencies or hidden scoring behaviour.
